  "rationale": "Every exfiltration technique (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) requires admin on db, fileserver or backup. Those need a foothold from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, and all three require stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin comes only from dump_dbadmin_dc (needs admin_dc) or dump_dbadmin_adfs (needs admin_adfs). admin_dc needs foothold_dc, and admin_adfs needs foothold_adfs. These footholds come only from auth_dc and auth_adfs, and both require NOT mfa_admin. Since mfa:admin is deployed, both are blocked. The attacker can still phish a workstation, pivot internally, authenticate to the appserver and apiserver, and kerberoast stolen_admin, but stolen_admin alone cannot get past mfa_admin. So stolen_dbadmin is never obtained and exfiltrated stays false."
